PEIOS-DIVERGENCE(maxdepth): raise libxslt's template-recursion limit.

DocBook's string.subst (docbook-xsl lib/lib.xsl) substitutes by recursing
once per match rather than by looping, so the template nesting depth of a
transform grows with the length of the string being escaped. Real documents
exceed libxslt's default limit of 3000 and abort with "a potential infinite
template recursion was detected" -- in the Linux tree, perf-c2c is the first
page large enough to do it, while the dozens of smaller perf pages render
fine, which is what distinguishes this from a genuine loop.

libxslt's own diagnostic names --maxdepth as the remedy. It is a
command-line flag with no environment equivalent, so there is nowhere to set
it from outside; xmlto has to pass it.

Upstreamable as-is: it raises a ceiling and changes no output.

--- a/xmlto.in
+++ b/xmlto.in
@@ -227,6 +227,11 @@
 # Disable network entities
 XSLTOPTS="$XSLTOPTS --nonet"
 
+# Raise the template-recursion limit. DocBook's string.subst recurses once
+# per match, so nesting depth grows with document length and the default of
+# 3000 is reached by ordinary reference pages.
+XSLTOPTS="$XSLTOPTS --maxdepth 20000"
+
 # The names parameter for the XSLT stylesheet
 XSLTPARAMS=""
 
